WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:08.008
Julianna she’s just fabulous to
work with.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.593
We have so much fun together.

00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:11.803
It can be very daunting going on
to another show

00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:13.722
that’s not yours, that’s already
been established.

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:15.766
But I knew Jen because we had
worked together and

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:17.309
come up together so she

00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:19.061
was a very welcome
sight for me.

00:00:19.269 --> 00:00:21.313
She was on E.R. and I was on
Friends, and our stage is

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:23.065
just like a stone’s throw away.

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:25.525
We used to go out and we’d
chat with each other.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:30.280
What was the nature of your
relationship with Mitch Kessler?

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:36.078
Seeing Laura go toe to toe with
Alex Levy is really fun because

00:00:36.078 --> 00:00:37.704
these are women
who have history.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.206
She’s very seasoned.

00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:41.166
Sophie and I, our costume
designer, talked about

00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.169
making her look a little bit
like Katherine Hepburn

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.338
with the turtleneck and the
white shirt.

00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:49.299
It was important to really
define her the very first time

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:52.803
we meet her on camera
and I needed her to have

00:00:52.803 --> 00:00:55.639
a sense of authority
and feel distinctly different

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:57.391
from the other women
on the show.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.851
Well if it isn’t Bradley Jackson

00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:03.021
Yup that’s me. I’ve heard so
much about you.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.899
Bradley is such an infinitely
curious person

00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:09.653
That she’s always pushing to
discover more about herself, so

00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:12.489
It felt so in character for
Bradley to be

00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:13.991
exploring her sexuality.

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:17.244
Reese said you never just
grab someone and kiss them

00:01:17.244 --> 00:01:20.497
whether you’re two women, two
men, a man and a woman,

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:23.041
and that’s when we did this
Sort of choreography where I

00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:25.252
said well if I put my hand up

00:01:25.252 --> 00:01:27.546
To your cheek and let you know
that I’m actually

00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:29.089
reciprocating the kiss.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.758
Then it will be something that’s
actually quite beautiful.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.344
Each character is in their own
world of achievement

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:38.682
and ambition and trying to get
ahead, meanwhile

00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:41.226
there’s this greater force of
nature about to shut

00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:44.938
everything down and we’re not
paying any attention.

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.232
Daniel we’ve gotta get out of
Wuhan before 10,

00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:48.191
they’re locking it down.

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:51.695
Creating Wuhan out of the
Anaheim train station

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:54.906
was insane, but it was
so beautifully done.

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:56.450
Wuhan has one train station

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.786
that had kind of an amazing hump
and then two smaller humps and

00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:01.830
I thought oh my gosh
the new metro link station

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.624
In Anaheim has that same
sort of shape to it.

00:02:05.042 --> 00:02:07.502
We were shooting the train
station really, really late

00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:11.673
at night, and literally I think
the train had to go off duty.

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:13.508
So when the train was done

00:02:13.508 --> 00:02:17.763
wherever it was, it came to us
and in 30 minutes, man,

00:02:17.763 --> 00:02:20.557
he had put up everything and
changed the signs and

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:23.769
what looked like just a regular,
uh, American train

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:25.812
became a train to Wuhan.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.647
(SPEAKING CHINESE)

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.357
He says we can’t

00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:29.691
Uh, tell him who we are

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:32.694
Daniel sees COVID first hand

00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:35.113
he's ringing the bell and no one
is listening.

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:37.741
And watching that
experience for him

00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:39.659
in this moment in time,

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.538
It really feels to resonant
and so relevant

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.706
and is really tremendous.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.166
♪♪

